<p id="S3.T1.3" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left ltx_figure_panel"><sup id="S3.T1.3.1" class="ltx_sup"><span id="S3.T1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:50%;">1</span></sup><span id="S3.T1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;"> Position sector: Center, Top-Left, Top-Right, Bottom-Left, Bottom-Right<span id="S3.T1.3.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our setup, each creative is passed through a set of eight <span id="S3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">child</span> MLLMs listed in the Table <a href="#S3.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ III Methodology ‣ M-PACE: Mother Child Framework for Multimodal Compliance" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>, which produce zero-shot predictions for each compliance task in a single forward pass. Zero-shot inference is particularly valuable in real world industry scenarios where latency and cost constraints make multi turn prompting impractical.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE II: </span>Major OpenAI and Google AI Models</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
